For a named valuable item (jewellery, watch, art, collectible) where the policy references a sub-limit or schedule cap for that category but does not state the figure, cap_uncertain does not license a zero estimate: still price the item at the tier implied by the description's own characterisation (e.g. "premium replacement watch" -> a frugal several-thousand-euro estimate, not the base model), the same way a stated brand or "luxury" wording is already priced. t_mid = 0 is only for not-covered/not-related items; an unknown cap is not that.

For separately invoiced skilled-worker, helper or service-technician hours, calculate the total using the full stated hour quantity at a conservative customary rate; do not substitute a guessed smaller number of hours merely because the repair is described as minor or straightforward, unless evidence specifically identifies hours as unrelated or excessive.

For specialist conservation, stabilisation or full restoration of a damaged painting, set t_low at no less than 95% of t_mid unless the file identifies a concrete scope uncertainty or disputed treatment.
